# Ingress with Traefik

Traefik is an Ingress Controller. It can be configured either through standard Kubernetes `Ingress` objects, or through its own CRDs (`IngressRoute`, `Middleware`), which are installed as part of the Helm chart.

## Install

Add the Traefik Helm repo and install the chart into its own namespace:

```bash
helm repo add traefik https://traefik.github.io/charts
helm repo update
```

```bash
helm install traefik traefik/traefik \
  --namespace traefik \
  --create-namespace \
  --set ports.web.exposedPort=80 \
  --set ports.websecure.exposedPort=443
```

Check the controller and IngressClass were created:

```bash
kubectl get pods -n traefik
kubectl get deployments -n traefik
kubectl get ingressclass
```

Get the external address assigned to the Traefik service (a `LoadBalancer` IP/hostname on a full cluster):

```bash
kubectl get svc traefik -n traefik
```

## Option A: standard `Ingress` resource

Traefik reads plain `Ingress` objects when `ingressClassName: traefik` is set. This is a drop-in replacement for the `ingress-nginx` example, routing to the same `nginx-clusterip-service`:

```yaml
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: nginx-ingress-traefik
  annotations:
    traefik.ingress.kubernetes.io/router.entrypoints: web
spec:
  ingressClassName: traefik
  rules:
  - host: nginx-traefik.example.com
    http:
      paths:
      - path: /
        pathType: Prefix
        backend:
          service:
            name: nginx-clusterip-service
            port:
              number: 80
```

```bash
kubectl apply -f examples/traefik/nginx_ingress_traefik.yaml
kubectl get ingress
kubectl describe ingress nginx-ingress-traefik
```

Point the hostname `nginx-traefik.example.com` at the external address of the Traefik service (via your DNS, or an `/etc/hosts` entry for local testing), then:

```bash
curl http://nginx-traefik.example.com
```

## Option B: native `IngressRoute` CRD

`IngressRoute` replaces the `Ingress` object with a Traefik-specific resource, using Traefik's own rule matching syntax (`Host()`, `PathPrefix()`, etc.) instead of the `rules`/`paths` structure:

```yaml
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: nginx-ingressroute
  namespace: default
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - web
  routes:
    - match: Host(`nginx-traefik.example.com`) && PathPrefix(`/`)
      kind: Rule
      services:
        - name: nginx-clusterip-service
          port: 80
```

```bash
kubectl apply -f examples/traefik/nginx_ingressroute.yaml
kubectl get ingressroute
kubectl describe ingressroute nginx-ingressroute
```

### Path rewrite via `Middleware`

`Middleware` is a separate CRD applied to routes for request/response manipulation. `stripPrefix` removes a path prefix before forwarding to the backend, equivalent to the `rewrite-target` annotation used with `ingress-nginx`:

```yaml
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: Middleware
metadata:
  name: strip-prefix
  namespace: default
spec:
  stripPrefix:
    prefixes:
      - /app
```

The middleware is referenced by name from the route that should use it:

```yaml
apiVersion: traefik.io/v1alpha1
kind: IngressRoute
metadata:
  name: nginx-ingressroute-rewrite
  namespace: default
spec:
  entryPoints:
    - web
  routes:
    - match: Host(`nginx-traefik.example.com`) && PathPrefix(`/app`)
      kind: Rule
      middlewares:
        - name: strip-prefix
      services:
        - name: nginx-clusterip-service
          port: 80
```

```bash
kubectl apply -f examples/traefik/middleware_strip_prefix.yaml
kubectl apply -f examples/traefik/nginx_ingressroute_rewrite.yaml
curl http://nginx-traefik.example.com/app/
```

A request to `/app/` arrives at the Pod as `/`, since the prefix is stripped by the middleware.

## Dashboard

Traefik exposes a web dashboard on port 9000 inside the pod, showing configured routers, services, and middlewares. It is not exposed externally by the chart by default, so use port-forwarding:

```bash
kubectl port-forward -n traefik $(kubectl get pods -n traefik -l app.kubernetes.io/name=traefik -o jsonpath='{.items[0].metadata.name}') 9000:9000
```

`http://127.0.0.1:9000/dashboard/`

## Cleanup

```bash
kubectl delete ingress nginx-ingress-traefik
kubectl delete ingressroute nginx-ingressroute nginx-ingressroute-rewrite
kubectl delete middleware strip-prefix
helm uninstall traefik -n traefik
kubectl delete namespace traefik
```

