## Minikube-specific notes

Only relevant if running this module against a local Minikube cluster instead of a full cluster.

### Multi-node taint workaround

If the control-plane node has the `NoSchedule` taint (as used earlier for `ingress-nginx`), the Traefik pod cannot be scheduled unless the taint is temporarily removed:

```bash
kubectl taint nodes minikube node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane:NoSchedule-
helm install traefik traefik/traefik \
  --namespace traefik \
  --create-namespace \
  --set ports.web.exposedPort=80 \
  --set ports.websecure.exposedPort=443
kubectl taint nodes minikube node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane:NoSchedule
```

### Lab proxy patch

Sets an external IP on the Traefik service so the lab's incoming proxy can reach it, same purpose as the equivalent patch on `ingress-nginx-controller`:

```bash
kubectl patch svc traefik -n traefik -p '{"spec": {"externalIPs": ["192.168.49.2"], "externalTrafficPolicy": ""}}'
```

### Resolving the hostname locally

`LoadBalancer` services have no real external IP on Minikube, so use the Minikube node IP instead and add it to `/etc/hosts`:

```bash
minikube ip
```

```text
192.168.49.2 nginx-traefik.example.com
```
